BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Altar Boys
DTSTART:20261024T010000Z
DTEND:20261024T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T010000Z
UID:DWx1sK9X4p
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival
  presents the film The Altar Boys. The story follows a group of altar bo
 ys who\, disillusioned by the Church's indifference\, decide to take matt
 ers into their own hands. They plant a bug in the confessional to learn th
 eir neighbors' secrets and dispense justice by their own rules. Their miss
 ion quickly spirals out of control. The screening will be followed by a Q
 &A with director Piotr Domalewski and actress Kamila Urzędowska.\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-polish-film-festival-2026/the-a
 ltar-boys\n\nEstimated start: 18:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bernstein's Wall (2021)
DTSTART:20261024T013000Z
DTEND:20261024T032500Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T013000Z
UID:gHSmgOueGk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nPerfectly timed after Spielberg
 ’s recent remake of West Side Story\, this portrait of its composer Leon
 ard Bernstein\, conqueror of both Broadway and the concert hall\, captures
  his genius and his voracious\, even self-destructive\, appetite for music
  and for life.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/bernsteins-wall
 \n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Whalefall
DTSTART:20261024T023000Z
DTEND:20261024T042500Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T023000Z
UID:1BGT9XNcH5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nFollowing the death of his father
  (Josh Brolin)\, Jay Gardiner (Austin Abrams) goes diving off the central 
 Coast of California in search of his remains\, but is swallowed by a massi
 ve sperm whale. While trapped inside its belly with only one hour of oxyge
 n left\, Jay comes to realize that the hard-earned lessons his father impa
 rted may be the key to his escape.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theat
 ers/whalefall\n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Erupcja
DTSTART:20261024T033000Z
DTEND:20261024T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20261024T033000Z
UID:fdtTpxwyFK
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 71 mins (1h11m)\n\nThe Seattle Polish Film Festival 
 presents the film Erupcja. A volcanic eruption strands Bethany and her 
 soon-to-be fiancé\, Rob\, in Warsaw\, Poland. Taking the explosive event 
 as a sign\, she soon reunites with her childhood friend\, Nel\, and embark
 s on a European adventure that forces her to confront the pains and pleasu
 res of growing up.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-poli
 sh-film-festival-2026/erupcja\n\nEstimated start: 20:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
