BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Glenn Canyon Institute's What the River Knows
DTSTART:20261023T020000Z
DTEND:20261023T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T020000Z
UID:Ax9t1stHXm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 34 mins (0h34m)\n\nPresented by Glen Canyon Institut
 e this Good Intentions Paving Co. documentary explores the reemergence of 
 Glen Canyon from the receding waters of Lake Powell reservoir. What the Ri
 ver Knows weaves together past and present to reveal the restoration of Gl
 en Canyon and a new way forward for the Colorado River. Following the film
  screening\, the event will conclude with a panel discussion and audience 
 Q+A.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/glen-canyon-institutes-wha
 t-the-river-knows\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wagon Master (1950)
DTSTART:20261023T020000Z
DTEND:20261023T034500Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T020000Z
UID:eiuUYacfjY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 86 mins (1h26m)\n\nTwo adventurous horse traders are
  hired to lead a Mormon wagon train through southeastern Utah\, forming a 
 community of outcasts as they travel along the dusty trail in John Ford’
 s lyrical road poem.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/the-open-
 road/wagon-master\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
